  ('3b13c23e-487d-5892-b1bf-7bad50fb6095', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the paragraph beginning "I do value silence" strengthen the conductor's argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By praising silence, he suggests that the musicians played poorly and that the audience should have stayed quiet out of politeness.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"By granting that silence has real power, he avoids seeming careless about tradition and narrows the dispute to how newcomers are treated.","is_correct":true},{"text":"By describing a held breath, he shifts the letter's topic from audience behavior to the breathing techniques of wind players.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"By admitting that silence is important, he reverses his earlier position and agrees that rules should be handed out at the door.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By granting that silence has real power, he avoids seeming careless about tradition and narrows the dispute to how newcomers are treated.$q$, $q$The concession shows he respects silence, then "But" pivots to his real point: never making first-time listeners afraid. He still rejects the idea of rules at the door, so this is a concession, not a reversal.$q$, 'draft', '1370c012-d480-57aa-95d6-66a089871fae')
